<article class="env-lemma" id="03F6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03F6">Lemma <span data-tag="03F6">21.10.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. An injective abelian sheaf is also injective as an object in the category $\textit{PAb}(\mathcal{C})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/015Z" data-tag="015Z">12.29.1</a> to the categories $\mathcal{A} = \textit{Ab}(\mathcal{C})$, $\mathcal{B} = \textit{PAb}(\mathcal{C})$, the inclusion functor and sheafification. (See Modules on Sites, Section <a href="/tag/03CM" data-tag="03CM">18.3</a> to see that all assumptions of the lemma are satisfied.) 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>